# Archiver Codebase

**Compact map for agents:** `model-archival/docs/AI_CONTEXT.md` and `model-archival/AGENTS.md` — read before whole-repo exploration.

**Cross-session context snapshot:** repo root **`.dump/CONTEXT_SNAPSHOT.md`** — user-maintained handoff; read when @-referenced or when the user asks to reload context (**`context-snapshot.mdc`**).

## Project structure

```
model-archival/
  scripts/run.sh      orchestrator — always use this to start downloads
  scripts/stop.sh     graceful shutdown — always use before rebooting
  config/
    registry.yaml     master model list (source of truth)
    drives.yaml       drive mount points and roles (includes **d5_vllm** → `/mnt/models/d1/vllm` for vLLM archiver slice)
  src/archiver/
    cli.py            click commands: download, verify, status, list, drives, tokens, pin, queue-plan, audit-tmp, failed-registry
    queue_plan.py     approximate queue order + per-drive free space (ENOSPC planning)
    downloader.py     per-model download logic (LFS via aria2, XET via hf_hub_download)
    scheduler.py      worker pool; max parallel models + max per drive; add more when speed/(n+1) >= 6 MB/s
    aria2_manager.py  aria2c daemon (16 concurrent files; optional --bandwidth-cap)
    state.py          run_state.json persistence (thread-safe)
    status.py         rich live UI + STATUS.md + RunReport
    models.py         ModelEntry / DriveConfig dataclasses + registry I/O
    verifier.py       SHA-256, manifest.json, global_index.jsonl
    preflight.py      pre-flight checks
vllm-hosting/
  config/vllm-archive-manifest.yaml   HF repos for vLLM archival (deduped from Ollama queue intent)
  scripts/vllm-archive-pull-one.sh     archive VM: one huggingface-cli download per run (optional trickle cap)
```

## Key bugs fixed in this session

- **`models.py` `model_dir`**: falls back to `"main"` when `commit_sha` is None — never returns None if `drive_path` is set
- **`state.py`**: `threading.Lock` protects `run_state.json`; writes via `.json.tmp` → rename
- **`aria2_manager.py`**: `--allow-overwrite=true`; removes orphaned partials (file exists but no `.aria2` control file) before submitting to aria2
- **`downloader.py`**: `GatedRepoError` + HTTP 401/403 raise `AuthError` immediately — no retry
- **`scheduler.py`**: SIGTERM/SIGINT sets `_stop_event`; workers stop cleanly between models
- **`scripts/run.sh`**: traps SIGTERM/SIGINT → forwards to Python child; writes `.archiver.pid`

## Design rules

- Downloads are always resumable — never delete `.tmp` partial files or `.aria2` control files
- Archiver infra (`run_state.json`, `logs/`, `archive/`, `STATUS.md`, `priority_overrides.json`, GDrive sentinel) lives on **D3**; **D5** only receives finished model trees when `drive: d5`. `.tmp` scratch: D1 preferred, then D3 — never D5.
- **Dynamic priority**: optional `priority_overrides.json` on D3 (infra root). JSON map `model_id -> priority` (lower = sooner). Re-read when picking each next model — edit the file anytime without restarting. Example: `{"meta-llama/Llama-3.3-70B-Instruct": 3}` defers that model until after priority-1/2.
- `commit_sha` in registry.yaml is auto-pinned after first download
- LFS CDN URLs expire ~1 hour — always re-fetch with `hf_hub_url()` before each attempt
- On SHA-256 mismatch: remove both the corrupt file AND its `.aria2` control file (force clean restart)
- `sync_archive()` replicates primary `archive/` (on D3) to **D1 and D2** only after each model completes (not D5)
- Concurrency: MAX_FILES_IN_FLIGHT=8 per model (downloader.py); ARIA2_MAX_CONCURRENT=16 (aria2_manager.py). Bandwidth cap (if set) is applied in aria2 only.

## Adding a model to registry.yaml

```yaml
org/ModelName:
  hf_repo: org/ModelName
  commit_sha: null        # auto-pinned on first download
  tier: A                 # A/B/C/D
  priority: 1             # 1 = base, 2 = smallest GGUF, 3 = instruct, 4 = middle quants (going forward)
  drive: d1
  requires_auth: false
  licence: Apache-2.0
  notes: "description"
```

## HF token

```bash
bash deploy/sethfToken.sh hf_YOURTOKEN   # stores in ~/.hf_token (chmod 600)
uv run archiver tokens check             # verify gated model access
```
